ed - edit text one line at a time

SYNOPSIS
    ed [-|-q] [file]

DESCRIPTION
    Use a to append, a single dot to end input, p to print, and s to
    substitute. Use w to write, q to quit, and Ctrl+C to return from
    an interrupted command. The editor ignores SIGQUIT unless started
    with -q. A bare ? reports a command error.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1)
